From acc0647a15128dea30f2f66a7453a340a1a5622a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mamaich <mamaich.eng@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:22:47 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] rg52mini: boot menu for a card with GammaOS and dArkOS

One card, two systems: GammaOS on the FAT named "dArkOS_Fat" (the name its
OTA packages write to) and dArkOS on "darkos_boot", the only bootable one.
When both are there with an extlinux.conf, rk_board_late_init() shows a
menu of ready-made pictures from the bootable FAT and boots the choice
with sysboot from its own FAT. The third item reboots into the eMMC with
the BOOT_EMMC flag, as "reboot emmc" does; it is shown only when GammaOS
keeps /bootmenu_emmc on its FAT, which follows the eMMC switch of its
Toolbox.

Until GammaOS has finished its setup wizard (/bootmenu_ready on its FAT)
the card boots straight into it: the wizard fills the ROMs folder that
dArkOS shares, and wipes RetroArch auto-saves there. Up or down held at
power-on brings the menu up anyway.

Keys: d-pad up (GPIO) and down (saradc1), volume up/down move; A, Start
or power boots. Five seconds without a key boot the default: the last
choice, kept in the Rockchip vendor storage of the card under an id of
our own and written only when it changes; GammaOS when there is none.

The menu stays out of recovery, loader, charging and "reboot emmc" (the
boot device check), and a card with one system boots as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
